# NSG UL reporting — the engine is no longer DL-only.
#
# Reference patch (distro trees are the source of truth; build-slim.sh bakes
# them). "The engine's known gap is UL" turned out to be wrong on two counts:
# the bearer stats calculator tracked UL all along (GetUlRxData & co — nothing
# read it), and the scenario simply carried no uplink traffic to measure.
#
# ── 1. scratch/scenario-zero-with_parallel_loging.cc ─────────────────────────
# Per-UE UPLINK traffic: each UE sends UDP to the remote host at 25% of its
# slice's DL rate (the usual asymmetry), 1400 B payload. ONE shared sink on
# the remote host, installed BEFORE the per-UE loop — installing it inside the
# loop re-binds the port for every UE after the first and aborts the sim at
# t=0 with "Failed to bind socket" (found the hard way).
#
# ── 2. contrib/oran-interface/helper/mmwave-indication-message-helper.{h,cc} ─
# AddCuUpUePmItem gains two optional params (default -1 = omit, so existing
# callers' messages stay byte-identical):
#   DRB.PdcpSduVolumeUl_Filter.UEID   uplink PDCP SDU volume (kbit) this period
#   DRB.PdcpSduBitRateUl.UEID         uplink bitrate (kbps)
#
# ── 3. src/mmwave/model/mmwave-enb-net-device.cc ─────────────────────────────
# BuildRicIndicationMessageCuUp: per UE,
#   nsgUlRxKbit = m_e2PdcpStatsCalculator->GetUlRxData (imsi, 3) * 8 / 1e3;
#   nsgUlKbps   = nsgUlRxKbit / m_e2Periodicity;
# passed into AddCuUpUePmItem. Read happens BEFORE ResetResultsForImsiLcid, so
# each report window is a fresh measurement, not a cumulative sum.
#
# Downstream needs NOTHING: the xApp decodes KPM names generically and
# engine_service collects every "name = value" pair, so the new metrics appear
# in kpm.measurements as DRB.PdcpSduVolumeUl / DRB.PdcpSduBitRateUl.
#
# ── VERIFIED on the real engine (2026-07-16) ─────────────────────────────────
# 10 UE / 5 gNB / 50 MHz, DL slice 10 Mbps (UL offered 2.5 Mbps/UE):
#   DRB.PdcpSduBitRateUl mean ~350 kbps, volume/bitrate self-consistent
#   (171 kbit / 0.5 s = 343 kbps).
# Demand doubled (DL 20 -> UL offered 5 Mbps): mean 761 kbps (~2.2x) — the
# measurement scales with offered load and sits well under the offered rate,
# i.e. it is a real mmWave TDD UL capacity measurement, not a config echo.
# Platform path: /ric/validate-nsoran returns both metrics (status=ok).

# ── ADDENDUM (2026-07-18): UL delay ──────────────────────────────────────────
# DRB.PdcpSduDelayUl.UEID added to the CU-UP per-UE items (GetUlDelay, same
# 0.1 ms unit as the DL delay). Measured on the real engine: 2.1-2.6 ms.
